{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeAnnihilates_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeAnnihilates_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L154-L161","doc":"If `J` satisfies the m-free annihilation at `q` for every `q`, it satisfies\nthe `q = 1` specialization. A trivial instantiation, but it anchors the\nconceptual bridge: the q → 1 limit of a q-holonomic sequence is holonomic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.IsQHolonomic_bar_of_mfree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.IsQHolonomic_bar_of_mfree","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L129-L145","doc":"**m-free q-holonomicity transports across bar.** If `J` is q-holonomic at\n`q` (via an m-free operator), then `J` is q-holonomic at `q⁻¹`. Sorry-free.\nThis is the general bar-transport lemma for the common case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.bar_annihilates_of_annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.bar_annihilates_of_annihilates","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L112-L127","doc":"**m-free bar duality.** If an m-free operator annihilates `J` at `q`, then\nits bar annihilates `J` at `q⁻¹`. This is the clean algebraic bar\ntransport: the m-independence means the annihilation condition `∑ c_j(q)\n· J(N+j) = r(q)` transforms to `∑ c_j(q⁻¹) · J(N+j) = r(q⁻¹)` by\nsimply replacing `q` with `q⁻¹` in the coefficients — and since the\nTower values `J(N+j)` don't change, this is the barred operator acting\non the SAME tower. Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.bar","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L106-L110","doc":"The bar involution of an m-free operator: replace `q` by `q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.annihilates_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.annihilates_iff","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L101-L104","doc":"m-free annihilation IS annihilation of the general operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeAnnihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeAnnihilates","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L96-L99","doc":"Annihilation for an m-free operator: `∑_j c_j(q) · J(N+j) = r(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.toOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.toOp","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L90-L94","doc":"Convert an m-free operator to the general `QDifferenceOperator`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.rhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.rhs","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Inhomogeneous RHS, depending only on `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.coeff","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Coefficient of the `j`-th shift, depending only on `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.order","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The order (shift-degree) of the operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.MFreeQDiffOp","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L78-L88","doc":"An **m-free** q-difference operator: one whose coefficients depend on\n`q` alone, not on the lattice variable `m`. The `Annihilates` relation\nfor such an operator uses `q^N` in the m-slot, but since the coefficients\nignore m, the annihilation condition simplifies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.of_bar_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.of_bar_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L61-L70","doc":"**q-Holonomicity transports for symmetric towers.** If `J(q⁻¹, ·)` is\nq-holonomic at `q⁻¹` and `J` is bar-symmetric at `q`, then `J(q, ·)` is\nalso q-holonomic at `q⁻¹`. Generalizes `coloredJones41_qholonomic_bar`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.annihilates_bar_of_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.annihilates_bar_of_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L47-L58","doc":"**Annihilation transports for symmetric towers.** If `op` annihilates\n`J(q⁻¹, ·)` at parameter `q⁻¹` and `J` is bar-symmetric at `q`, then\n`op` also annihilates `J(q, ·)` at `q⁻¹`. Sorry-free; the proof\nsubstitutes `J q = J q⁻¹` as functions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.IsBarSymmetric.eq_fun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.IsBarSymmetric.eq_fun","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L42-L45","doc":"Bar symmetry gives function-level equality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.IsBarSymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarTransport.IsBarSymmetric","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarTransport.lean#L35-L40","doc":"A tower `J` (indexed by a parameter `q : K` and a color `n : ℕ`) is\nbar-symmetric at `q` if its values at `q` and `q⁻¹` coincide pointwise.\nThis holds for amphichiral knots (like `4₁`) where the colored Jones\npolynomial is invariant under `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}